    24	it is exactly as good as "a uniformly random ideal of norm about √|Δ_K|", and in every field we can use for
    25	factoring that norm is a power of N. The obstruction is not ERH-shaped at all. Below L[2/5] a descent must create
    26	algebraic children (prime ideals of the field it works in), and these can only be descended in that same field; a
    27	proof then needs control of one fixed polynomial's values at more points than the field has random parameters.
    28	No tool for that exists, with or without ERH. Under ERH plus one clean pointwise hypothesis (AD: every target in
    29	range has a good box point) the whole L[1/3] algorithm *is* rigorous, with every other step (tree, costs,
    30	recursion, transcript invariance, linear algebra) proved here; ERH is used only for the character columns.
    31	Best α under ERH from this work: **α = 1/2** (no improvement). L[1/3] factoring, rigorous or ERH-conditional, is not
