   486	## 10. Literature (literature subagent and codex nested_1, primary sources where marked)
   487	
   488	- **Factoring.** Rigorous record L[1/2, 1 + o(1)]: Lenstra–Pomerance, JAMS 5 (1992) 483–516 (read; Thm 6.1 p. 499
   489	  read in the original scan). Earlier: Pomerance 1987 L[1/2, √2]; Vallée L[1/2, √(4/3)]. Nothing below 1/2,
   490	  rigorous or GRH-conditional, 1990–2026 (searches). Lee–Venkatesan, JNT 187 (2018), arXiv 1805.08873 (read): Thm 2.1
   491	  unconditional L[1/3, (64/9)^{1/3}] for a congruence x² ≡ y² that "may be trivial" (Remark 2.2); Thm 2.3
   492	  nontriviality only for N = pq, p ≡ q ≡ 3 (mod 4), under their Conjecture 7.1. Their relation collection uses HECM
   493	  (lv6 §6.5).
   494	- **Discrete logs.** Rigorous L[1/2, √2] for F_p and F_{2^n} (Pomerance 1987). Kleinjung–Wesolowski, JAMS 35 (2022),
   495	  arXiv 1906.10668: rigorous (pn)^{2log₂n+O(1)} in F_{p^n}, hence rigorous L(α) for p = L_{p^n}(α), α < 1/2 (their
   496	  corollary); also Granger–Kleinjung–Zumbrägel (Trans. AMS 2018), Lido (arXiv 2206.10327). The mechanism (Frobenius
   497	  model; each elimination step is a point count on an explicit curve, Weil bounds; smoothness of polynomials is exact
   498	  counting) has no analogue for integers. No rigorous L(α < 1/2) in medium/large characteristic.
   499	- **Class groups.** Hafner–McCurley 1989 (ERH, imaginary quadratic, L(1/2, √2)); dBPW 2025/26 (ERH, all fields,
   500	  L_{|Δ|}(1/2)); Biasse (Math. Comp. 2014, arXiv 0912.1927; arXiv 1204.1292) L(1/3) for special families, heuristic;
   501	  Biasse–Fieker (LMS JCM 2014) GRH + heuristics.
   502	- **Jacobians.** Enge–Gaudry–Thomé (arXiv 0905.2177): L(1/3), heuristic (Heuristics 5–6 cover relation collection
   503	  and the special-Q descent). Rigorous results are L(1/2)-type (Enge 2002, Enge–Gaudry 2002, Couveignes 2001, Hess
   504	  2004) or fixed-genus powers (Diem, Math. Comp. 2011).
   505	- **Smooth values / linear systems.** BBDT (Comment. Math. Helv. 2012): y ≥ x^{g−2+ε} for binary forms of degree g;
   506	  Tenenbaum–Wu (2003): L-type smoothness only for binary *quadratic* forms; one-variable polynomials of degree ≥ 2:
   507	  no L-type results (de la Bretèche–Drappeau). Harper (Compositio) a + b = c for y ≥ (log x)^K; Matthiesen–Wang
   508	  (ANT 2025) Ψ > N/log⁸N; Lachand (Acta Arith. 2017) fixed u.
   509	- **GRH and smooth numbers in progressions.** Pointwise asymptotics are known for q ≤ y^{4√e−δ} (Soundararajan 2008;
   510	  Harper JNT 2012), on average up to x^{1/2+} (Harper; Drappeau; Pascadi). A pointwise GRH statement for q ≫ y was
   511	  not found (the literature agent suggests one may follow from Harper's Prop. 1 + GRH; unchecked, not used).
   512	- **Family-averaged GRH.** Pierce–Turnage-Butterbaugh–Wood (Invent. Math. 2020), Lemke Oliver–Thorner–Zaman (2024):
   513	  fixed degree, fixed Galois group only.
   514	- No prior statement of Theorem AF's two-sided form, of Prop SI, or of Theorem NR was found by us; Prop SI(i) is also in
   515	  codex nested_1 ((19)), found independently.
