   517	## 11. Answers to the task, item by item
   518	
   519	1. dBPW: §1. Two-sided values with a shared rational side are outside its scope; its level structure is a single
   520	   sampling step; its cofactor scale is ≥ √|Δ_K| (Theorem AF), N^{Θ(1)} for factoring fields.
   521	2. Designs: (a) ideal-class descent on the algebraic side with a randomised rational side: the rational side is not
   522	   independent of the field once ψ is fixed (g₀ ≡ mg₁ mod N; codex (20)), and the algebraic step is dBPW-type
   523	   (Theorem AF); (b) inductive good sets: well defined (codex (17)) but their density is exactly the open statement,
   524	   and (log N)^{−C} per level is not enough (Prop BT); (c) dBPW at each level: no contraction (Cor AF); (d) fresh
   525	   fields: rational children yes (Prop R), algebraic no (Lemma FB), floor 2/5 (Prop R2).
   526	3. Costs: tree e^{O(log² t)} nodes, recursion closes (Theorem NR's proof); the size model is right, the supply is
   527	   not proved.
   528	4. (T): Lemma T_multi, proved for adaptive multi-level trees with restarts.
   529	5. ERH: needed for LV6 characters at growing degree (Lemma X_ERH), avoidable via LV §6; not the missing input for
   530	   nested descent; no family-averaged replacement exists for growing degree.
   531	6. Literature: §10. L[1/3] under ERH for factoring is not known.
   532	
   533	**Best α under ERH: 1/2.** (Unconditional L[1/2, 1] by LP92; internally L[1/2, o(1)] by RA + P, unrefereed.)
   534	**Sharpest barrier:** a quantitative supply of short two-sided special-q relations whose children lie in the
   535	recursively defined good sets *of the same field*. Equivalently (Theorem NR), Hypothesis AD. It is pointwise in one
   536	fixed field (Prop SI, Prop OD), it cannot come from Arakelov-uniform sampling (Theorem AF), and ERH does not address
   537	it.
