   543	## 13. Candidate card
   544	
   545	- **Mechanism.** ERH-conditional nested descent for the recursive Dixon-descent factoring algorithm, via dBPW sampling,
   546	  fresh fields, or inductive good sets.
   547	- **Model.** Theorem A / recurse architecture, one field of degree δD′, O(log log N) levels.
   548	- **Result.** No rigorous α < 1/2 under ERH. Proved: Theorem AF (dBPW's sampler is exactly "random ideal of norm
   549	  ≥ √|Δ_K|"), Prop SI (sparse-image dilemma), Lemma FB, Lemma OD, Lemma X_ERH, Lemmas RW/TS/T_multi, and Theorem NR
   550	  (ERH + AD + LV6′ ⇒ L[1/3, c_NR]).
   551	- **Failure scope.** All designs whose children include algebraic primes of the descending field (necessary below
   552	  2/5); all Arakelov-uniform samplers; all field-moment methods beyond depth 1.
   553	- **Next step.** Either a pointwise (fixed-field) L-scale smoothness theorem for binary forms on special-q lattices,
   554	  or a non-descent source of hidden randomness at L[1/3]. Neither is in sight.

